From 6beecdcfa00ac4d635425f17d787149f4b3ba240 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 11:23:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 40/98] contrib: glib2 (GLib 2.56.4) + automake-pyshim (GTK+
 2.x foundation)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GLib 2.56.4 — the last autotools GLib, chosen because its glib-genmarshal/
glib-mkenums/glib-compile-resources are Python scripts that run on the build
host (no target-exec generator step).  Cross-built via the substrate-autotools
helpers against dist-zlib + dist-libffi; --with-pcre=internal (no PCRE port),
NLS resolves to substrate libc's gettext.  Produces glib/gobject/gio/gmodule/
gthread .so + .pc.

gcc16: -std=gnu11 (GLib predates C23's `bool` keyword) and
--enable-compile-warnings=no (drops GLib's hardcoded -Werror=format-overflow,
which gcc16 raises on null %s args in gdbus*.c).

automake-pyshim/imp.py: a tiny `imp` shim (get_tag/cache_from_source ->
importlib) for `make install`.  2018-era automake's py-compile imports `imp`,
removed in Python 3.12; reusable by the other GNOME ports (pango/atk).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
